  <static seed="1761" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/SignedNumbersArithemtic/DivideWithNegativeIntegers20.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following. 
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\frac{-2}{-1}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{10}{-1}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{200}{-200}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{-18}{-18}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{19}{0}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{0}{-7}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{undefined}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The rules for determining the sign of the result when dividing positive and negative numbers are the same as those for multiplication:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{positive} \div \text{positive} = \text{positive} }</m>,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{positive} \div \text{negative} = \text{negative} }</m>,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{negative} \div \text{positive} = \text{negative} }</m>,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{negative} \div \text{negative} = \text{positive} }</m>.</p>
<p>In addition, <m>0</m> divided by any number (except <m>0</m>) is <m>0</m>; any number divided by <m>0</m> is undefined.</p>
<p>The solutions are:</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{-2}{-1}={2},  }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{10}{-1}={-10},  }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{200}{-200}={-1},  }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{-18}{-18}={1},  }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{19}{0}  }</m> is undefined</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{0}{-7}={0}.  }</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
